  <data name="sites_return_site" xml:space="preserve"><value>Return to Site</value><comment>The same command in the Mac&apos;s menu bar while there is nothing for it to do (the tab in front is no Site, or is at its home): shown grey.</comment></data>
  <data name="sites_site" xml:space="preserve"><value>Site</value><comment>Said of a tab that is kept, to a screen reader, with the tab&apos;s name.</comment></data>
  <data name="sites_sleep" xml:space="preserve"><value>Put to Sleep</value><comment>Label of the button at the end of a Site&apos;s tab, where another tab has Close Tab: the Site&apos;s page is closed and the Site stays in the row.</comment></data>
  <data name="space_automatic_colour" xml:space="preserve"><value>If you choose none, it gets one that no other Space has.</value><comment>Under the colours on the page that makes a Space.</comment></data>
  <data name="space_chip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Space: {0}</value><comment>Accessibility name of the button at the start of the strip of tabs that says which Space the window shows, and opens the list of Spaces. %@ is the Space&apos;s name.</comment></data>
  <data name="space_chosen_colour" xml:space="preserve"><value>Colour: {0}</value><comment>The same heading when a colour is chosen: it names the colour in words, so that it is not told by the colour alone. %@ is the colour&apos;s name, such as Blue.</comment></data>
