  <data name="switcher_open" xml:space="preserve"><value>Tabs: {0}</value><comment>Accessibility label of a button in the toolbar of a narrow window (a phone&apos;s): it opens the switcher, a sheet with every tab of the row. %d is how many tabs the row has; the button itself shows that number alone.</comment></data>
  <data name="switcher_title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Tabs</value><comment>Title at the head of the switcher, the sheet on a phone that lists every tab of the row.</comment></data>
  <data name="tab_empty_hint" xml:space="preserve"><value>Type an address or a search above.</value><comment>Hint under the heading of an empty tab.</comment></data>
  <data name="tab_empty_title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Where to?</value><comment>Heading of a tab that has no page yet.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_close" xml:space="preserve"><value>Close Tab</value><comment>Button on a tab in the strip, and command (Command-W on a Mac): close the tab.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_list" xml:space="preserve"><value>Tabs</value><comment>Accessibility label of the strip of the window&apos;s tabs.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_move_down" xml:space="preserve"><value>Move Tab Down</value><comment>The same command with the tabs down the side of the window: the tab changes places with the one below it.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_move_left" xml:space="preserve"><value>Move Tab Left</value><comment>Command for a tab drawn in a row along the top, or a Favourite&apos;s tile (in the Mac&apos;s Window menu, for the tab in front; in a tab&apos;s own menu on a touch screen): the tab changes places with the one on its left. Grey when no tab of its kind is on that side.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_move_right" xml:space="preserve"><value>Move Tab Right</value><comment>The same command the other way: the tab changes places with the one on its right.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_move_up" xml:space="preserve"><value>Move Tab Up</value><comment>The same command with the tabs down the side of the window: the tab changes places with the one above it.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_new" xml:space="preserve"><value>New Tab</value><comment>Button at the end of the strip of tabs, and command (Command-T on a Mac): open an empty tab.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_next" xml:space="preserve"><value>Show Next Tab</value><comment>Command in the Mac&apos;s Window menu (Control-Tab): bring the next tab in the row in front; from the last, the first.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_previous" xml:space="preserve"><value>Show Previous Tab</value><comment>Command in the Mac&apos;s Window menu (Control-Shift-Tab): bring the tab before in the row in front; from the first, the last.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_reopen" xml:space="preserve"><value>Reopen Closed Tab</value><comment>Command (Shift-Command-T on a Mac): bring back the tab that was last closed, where it was.</comment></data>
  <data name="tabs_untitled" xml:space="preserve"><value>New Tab</value><comment>The name the strip gives a tab that has no page yet.</comment></data>
  <data name="toolbar_back" xml:space="preserve"><value>Back</value><comment>Button: go back one page.</comment></data>
  <data name="toolbar_forward" xml:space="preserve"><value>Forward</value><comment>Button: go forward one page.</comment></data>
  <data name="toolbar_open_location" xml:space="preserve"><value>Open Location</value><comment>Command (Command-L on a Mac): put the keyboard in the address field with the whole address selected.</comment></data>
  <data name="toolbar_reload" xml:space="preserve"><value>Reload</value><comment>Button: reload the page.</comment></data>
  <data name="toolbar_stop" xml:space="preserve"><value>Stop</value><comment>Button: stop loading the page.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_arrangement" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo</value><comment>Command (Command-Z on a Mac, in the Edit menu; at the top of a tab&apos;s or a Group&apos;s own menu on a touch screen): undo the newest thing done to arrange the row of tabs, when the app has no words for what that was; and on a Mac the same item when it undoes typing in a field.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_favourite_added" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo Add to Favourites</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a tab having been made a Favourite.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_favourite_removed" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo Remove from Favourites</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a Favourite having been made an ordinary Site again.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_group_coloured" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo Group Colour</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a Group having been given another colour.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_group_made" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo New Group</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a Group having been made.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_group_moved" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo Move to Group</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a tab having been put in a Group, or taken out of one.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_group_removed" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo Remove Group</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a Group having been removed.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_group_renamed" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo Rename Group</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a Group having been given another name.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_group_reordered" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo Move Group</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a Group having been moved among the Groups.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_site_kept" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo Keep as Site</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a tab having been kept as a Site.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_site_let_go" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo Stop Keeping</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a Site having been let go.</comment></data>
  <data name="undo_tab_moved" xml:space="preserve"><value>Undo Move Tab</value><comment>The same command when what it undoes is a tab having been moved to another place in its row.</comment></data>
  <data name="zoom_done" xml:space="preserve"><value>Done</value><comment>Button that closes the zoom bar.</comment></data>
  <data name="zoom_in" xml:space="preserve"><value>Zoom In</value><comment>Button in the zoom bar, and the command (Command-plus on a Mac): make the page bigger.</comment></data>
  <data name="zoom_level" xml:space="preserve"><value>{0}%</value><comment>The zoom bar&apos;s level, in per cent. %ld is the number; %% is a per cent sign.</comment></data>
  <data name="zoom_open" xml:space="preserve"><value>Zoom</value><comment>Label of the button, beside the tabs, that opens the zoom bar.</comment></data>
  <data name="zoom_out" xml:space="preserve"><value>Zoom Out</value><comment>Button in the zoom bar, and the command (Command-minus on a Mac): make the page smaller.</comment></data>
  <data name="zoom_reset" xml:space="preserve"><value>Actual Size</value><comment>Accessibility label of the zoom bar&apos;s level, which puts the page back to 100% when pressed; and the command (Command-0 on a Mac).</comment></data>
</root>
